            "text": "At the Millbeck bridge a painted board hangs on a new post, with a wax seal at the bottom. A man in a clean coat sits under it with a ledger. The toll belongs to a Saltmouth company now, he says: the same two silver a head, written down this time.",
            "note": "Before the choices, say in one plain sentence what happened here last time: who held the bridge and what the Blades did about it. Something learned goes out of date: the brothers' false toll is now a true one, on paper, and the paper is Rufus's company's. The clerk is not a villain; he is paid by the day, like the Blades. If the brothers were spared, he has never heard of them. Bren respects a seal; Ilsa asks who gave the company the bridge.",
